### Exceptions (Dynamic Linking)
FrameForge dynamically links against the following LGPL-licensed libraries.
Per LGPL Section 6, you may use FrameForge with proprietary applications
provided you:
1. Use dynamic linking (shared libraries)
2. Allow users to swap the LGPL libraries
3. Provide build instructions for the LGPL components

| Library | License | Linkage |
|---------|---------|---------|
| libmpv | LGPL-2.1+ | Dynamic |
| FFmpeg (libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libswscale, libswresample, libavfilter) | LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2+ | Dynamic |
| GTK3 / WebKitGTK | LGPL-2.1+ | Dynamic |
| libva / VAAPI | MIT / LGPL | Dynamic |

### GPL Components (If Linked)
The following are GPL-licensed and will trigger GPL if **statically linked**:
- x264 (GPL)
- x265 (GPL)
- libaom (BSD-2, but patent considerations)

**FrameForge does not statically link these by default.** They are accessed
via FFmpeg's dynamic plugin system or not used (software fallback uses
FFmpeg's internal encoders which may be LGPL depending on build config).

### Codec Patents
H.264/AVC, H.265/HEVC, and other codecs may be subject to patents in some
jurisdictions. **Patent licensing is the responsibility of the end user
and/or distributor in their jurisdiction.** FrameForge makes no patent
grants or warranties.

